  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 0.0,
      "e": 2.0,
      "text": "Okay, so here we go."
    },
    {
      "s": 2.0,
      "e": 10.32,
      "text": "So as you can see, you get nice and tight all around here."
    },
    {
      "s": 10.32,
      "e": 12.2,
      "text": "You see I have no room here."
    },
    {
      "s": 12.2,
      "e": 15.16,
      "text": "So what it's doing is it's actually locking my helmet into place."
    },
    {
      "s": 15.16,
      "e": 17.52,
      "text": "I can't actually move anywhere."
    },
    {
      "s": 17.52,
      "e": 21.0,
      "text": "The whole helmet gets locked in."
    },
    {
      "s": 21.0,
      "e": 24.0,
      "text": "It's the same plate I want to show you."
    },
    {
      "s": 24.0,
      "e": 32.9,
      "text": "One of the people out there that still choose to not wear helmets is obviously if I just"
    },
    {
      "s": 32.9,
      "e": 34.7,
      "text": "had a skid litter, I have this."
    },
    {
      "s": 34.7,
      "e": 38.94,
      "text": "My head's going all over the place while I'm bouncing off guardrails for this."
    },
    {
      "s": 38.94,
      "e": 42.94,
      "text": "So obviously it's meant to be, it's like airbags in your car."
    },
    {
      "s": 42.94,
      "e": 45.18,
      "text": "It's meant to work with your seat belt."
    },
    {
      "s": 45.18,
      "e": 46.18,
      "text": "So save the helmets."
    }
